review_comments:
Yes - 2 minor releases (1.22, 1.23).

In 1.22 we have to validate Create() and Update() differently:

```
create:
    // TODO: after 1.22, change this to MaxDNSSearchPaths, get rid of legacy
    if len(dnsConfig.Searches) > MaxDNSSearchPathsLegacy {
        // error
    }
```

```
update:
    // TODO: after 1.22, change this to simply check MaxDNSSearchPaths
    maxSearchPaths := MaxDNSSearchPathsLegacy
    if len(old.dnsConfig.Searches) > MaxDNSSearchPathsLegacy {
        // special case - probably a rollback from the future
        maxSearchPaths = MaxDNSSearchPaths
    }
    if len(new.dnsConfig.Searches) > maxSearchPaths {
        // error
    }
```     

Similar for MaxDNSSearchListChars.

This allows someone to upgrade to 1.23, use this new limit, then roll back to 1.22 and not explode.
